rs found thatcosts of groceries,gasandhealthcareare among the top pain points for rural voters. They are also more likely than voters overall to say they are worried about being able to afford groceries or gas.Rural Americans skew Republican and historically have been an instrumental voting bloc for Trump. The findings suggest that many rural voters haven’t turned against Trump but that they also largely don’t think he has delivered on his economic promises. While rural voters seem unlikely to support Democrats on a large scale, Trump and the Republican Party could face challenges with them in November.The full story can be readher...", "published_at": "2026-09-23T13:57:23+00:00", "image_url": null, "source": {"name": "Fast Company", "tier": "independent", "url": "https://www.fastcompany.com"}, "bias_scores": [{"political_lean": 36, "sensationalism": 18, "opinion_fact": 31, "factual_rigor": 13, "framing": 13, "confidence": 0.49, "rationale": {"lean": {"keyword_score": 50.0, "framing_shift": 0.0, "entity_shift": 0.9, "sentence_direction": 0.0, "text_score": 50.9, "source_baseline": 35, "text_shift": 0.9, "delta_max": 10, "confidence": 1.0, "top_left_keywords": [], "top_right_keywords": [], "framing_phrases_found": [], "entity_sentiments": {"trump": 0.03, "donald trump": -0.02, "republicans": -0.02, "republican": -0.05, "democrats": -0.1}, "state_affiliated": false, "unscored": false}, "sensationalism": {"headline_score": 0.3, "body_score": 8.8, "clickbait_signals": 0, "superlative_density": 0.0, "urgency_density": 0.0, "hyperbole_density": 0.0, "measured_density": 0.0, "partisan_attack_density": 0.0}, "opinion": {"pronoun_score": 0.0, "subjectivity_score": 32.4, "modal_score": 0.0, "hedging_score": 0.0, "attribution_score": 75.0, "metadata_score": 0.0, "value_judgment_score": 0.0, "absolutist_assertion_score": 0.0, "classification": "Analysis", "dominant_signals": ["attribution_gaps", "subjectivity"]}, "coverage": {"named_sources_count": 1, "org_citations_count": 0, 